  "summary": "DIR-071 COMPLETE. (1) OPTIONAL AUTH: backend/security/auth.js now exports optionalAuth plus two shared helpers (bearerTokenFrom, resolveUser). requireAuth and optionalAuth build the IDENTICAL frozen req.user shape; optionalAuth decodes a present Bearer token and ALWAYS calls next() - it never 401s and grants no permission, so a public surface stays public. (2) WIRING: backend/index.js imports optionalAuth and the /api public-path branch now runs it, so req.user is finally populated on /api/public-export and /api/public-export-docx. ROOT CAUSE PROVEN: the DIR-069 employer claim at index.js:4448 (if (req.user?.uid) was DEAD CODE - public paths returned next() without ever decoding a token, and the PDF route had no claim branch at all, so a recruiter exporting a draft applicant always hit the 404. (3) ONE SHARED CLAIM: the verification rules moved into backend/security/employerClaim.js and are called by BOTH routes, so the PDF and DOCX authorization can never drift. A claim requires req.user.uid, repo.getJob(jobId).employerId === user.uid, an application bound to that job AND referencing exactly this resumeId, and a resolvable applicant id; it then returns the candidate ACTUAL applied resume from repo.getResume(applicantId, resumeId) with ownerUid = the applicant. Anything else returns null and the strict published-only rule (isPublished true, publicationMode explicit) is unchanged. ZERO IDOR: no client value is trusted as authority, and the employer id, job id, application id and resume id must all agree server-side. (4) CLIENT: EmployerApplicantPipeline.jsx now sends withAuth: true and passes jobId (jobId ?? job_id) and applicationId (applicationId ?? application_id ?? id), keeping the existing loading and role=status error surfaces. (5) PHOTO VISIBILITY: photo is null whenever showPhoto is false OR hidePhoto is true OR includePhoto is false, enforced at all four boundaries - src/cv-templates/templateUtils.js (the template view model), src/utils/resumeData.js normalizeResumeData, MySQLRepository._resumeSnapshot (so a hidden photo can never reach a public publication snapshot), and the builder export path (BuildResume.jsx now hands persistLatest to downloadResumePdf and downloadResumeDocx so the CURRENT visibility state is persisted at export time). VERIFIED EVIDENCE: DIR-063..071 suites 84/84 pass (dir071 is 12/12 - 5 static contracts + 7 functional proofs including a FOREIGN employer, a mismatched resumeId, an application bound to another job, anonymous callers, malformed ids and throwing readers all rejected, plus a photo matrix proving null under every hiding flag and preserved under showPhoto true); copilot-command-surface 28/28 after re-scoping INV-1; lint 0 errors; test:security static 67 + backend 897 pass; test:product exit 0; test:templates exit 0; test:xampp-policy exit 0; the DIR-070 void probe still passes; warm build 3.39s (budget < 4.0s). SUPERSEDED CONTRACTS REPORTED HONESTLY (4): mandate 4A requires editing src/cv-templates/templateUtils.js while mandate 5 requires src/cv-templates to stay git diff 0 - those cannot both hold as written. templateUtils.js is the SHARED UTILITY, not one of the 55 frozen template modules, so I made the mandated edit and RE-SCOPED the freeze to the 55 template modules (cv1..cv51, cover1..cover4), which are provably unchanged: git diff --name-only over src/cv-templates/cv* and cover* = 0 files, and only templateUtils.js differs (1 file). The release manifest now records the scope explicitly and tracks the shared utility separately (frozenBaseline.clean true, sharedUtility.changedByDirective true) instead of silently widening the freeze; tests/copilot-command-surface.test.mjs INV-1 now asserts the template MODULES are byte-identical AND that nothing else under src/cv-templates changed unnoticed; tests/dir068 and dir069 assert the same scoped contract. DIR-067 S1/S4, DIR-068 and DIR-069 S6/S7 were updated where DIR-071 intentionally reverses them (withAuth false to true, the claim rules moving into the shared module, and the robust applicationId chain). NO IDOR WEAKENING: the published-only fallback, the entitlement gate, the watermark logic and the rate limiters are all untouched, and optionalAuth cannot elevate because it only sets req.user. src/cv-templates template modules remain byte-identical, no detached server was spawned (XAMPP-only, xampp-policy green), and no Windows-only tooling was introduced."
}